// THE GAME'S WATER: a lake laid in one call on the wind (ge::water; skill: water). Everything
// anything asks of it, the physics, a swimmer, the sound and a picture, goes through
// `ge::water::sample`, so none of them can disagree about where the surface is.
//
// The world is data, built once: hold it beside the GameState (never inside it: it is not part
// of a run's digest, the seed and the time say everything about a lake) and hand it to whatever
// asks. Each fixed step, `ge::water::step(world, kDt)` steps what moves on its own (the flow
// regions; a lake's waves are a pure function of the time). Ask it with
// `ge::water::sample(world, x, y, z, t)`: the surface, its normal and velocity, the depth, the
// bed, the foam.
//
// To make it yours: move the shore, the level and the bed to your world's; pick a look by name
// (`ge::water::looks()`: the colour is what is in the water); add an ocean, a river, a volume or
// a flow region beside it (add_ocean, add_river, add_volume, add_flow). The lab pictures it.
//
// ge:summary The game's water: a lake laid in one call on the wind, and its bed
// ge:keywords water lake add_lake sample wind look bed shore
// ge:keywords {{snake}}
// ge:keywords make_{{snake}}
// ge:skill water
// ge:test tests/sim_{{snake}}_test.cpp
#pragma once

#include "water/world.hpp"

namespace {{ident}}::sim {

// The lake's surface, m (world y), and the deepest its bed goes under it.
inline constexpr double kLakeLevel = 0.0;
inline constexpr double kLakeDeepest = 6.0;

// The water, under a wind of `wind_mps` (10 m over the lake) blowing from +z toward -z.
ge::water::World make_{{snake}}(double wind_mps = 7.0);

}  // namespace {{ident}}::sim
